course: dictionary
lesson: 5271
title: Words that name a control
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A joystick is a lever you push in any direction. You can find out what it means from the words around it. «In an experiment pigs learned to move a joystick with their snouts to hit a target on a screen.» You move it, and it hits a target on a screen, so a joystick must be something you move to control things.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit in the gap? «In one study even steered a joystick with their snouts to play a simple computer game.» Steered means guided, and the game tells you the joystick is used to control something. Now swap your meaning in: "pigs pushed a lever to play a game" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. A joystick can also be the control stick of an aeroplane, which the pilot uses to steer it. The words around it tell you which meaning is being used: a game, a machine or a plane.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Joystick» means a lever that you push in any direction to control a video game, a computer or a machine.
fact: A joystick can also be the control stick of an aeroplane, used by the pilot to steer it.
fact: In computing, a joystick is an «input device», like a mouse or keyboard.
fact: In one study, pigs used a joystick with their snouts to play a simple computer game.
exercise: «Pigs learned to move a joystick with their snouts to hit a target on a screen.» What is a joystick? | *A lever you push to control a game or machine | A kind of food for pigs | A type of screen | A farm animal
exercise: «In one study even steered a joystick with their snouts to play a simple computer game.» Which word tells you the pig was controlling the joystick? | pigs | study | snouts | *steered
exercise: A pilot uses a joystick to steer an aeroplane. What does the pilot use the joystick for? | To feed the pigs | To read a map | To cook dinner | *To steer the aeroplane
test: «Pigs can play simple video games with a joystick, and they find buried food with their noses.» What does a joystick let you do? | *Control a game or machine by pushing it | Keep a bed clean | Dig up buried food | Hear quiet sounds
test: In computing, what kind of thing is a joystick? | *An input device, like a mouse or keyboard | A kind of battery | A loud bell | A type of pig
exam: Which sentence uses joystick correctly, as in the wheelchair example? | He put the joystick in the oven | She drank a joystick for breakfast | *She steered her powered wheelchair with a joystick | The joystick was very old and covered in moss
